<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Magic Portals Enhanced on Android (planning step 203, PORT-5): the engine's SupersonicActivity, a NativeActivity with a few lines of Java for what
    only the UI thread may do (hiding the system bars, reporting the window's safe area; engine/src/platform/android/java/, compiled into classes.dex by
    tools/package/android_package.py). The platform loads libMagicPortals.so (android.app.lib_name), whose android_main is the engine's
    (engine/src/platform/android/AndroidApp.cpp) and which calls game/android/AndroidMain.cpp's SupersonicMain.

    NOT RUN ON A PHONE OR AN EMULATOR as of this step: built, packaged and statically checked.

    WHAT IS NOT IN THIS FILE, ON PURPOSE.
      - versionName and versionCode. versionName is the ONE version definition, project(MagicPortals VERSION ...) in the top-level CMakeLists.txt,
        and versionCode is a whole number that goes up by one with every release (or Android refuses the update): the packager hands both to aapt2,
        which writes them in (its version-name and version-code options), so neither is spelled twice.
      - permissions. The game needs none: no INTERNET, no storage (its files are in its own private folder; the APK's data is unpacked there).
      - the launcher icon's pictures: tools/art/make_app_icon.py draws them at package time (nothing of the kind is committed).
    THE APPLICATION ID below is a PLACEHOLDER the owner confirms before anything is published: an id is permanent once an app is on a store. It differs
    from the original game's and from the sibling port's.

    minSdk 26 is where AAudio begins (the engine's audio on Android). The game needs a Vulkan 1.1 device (uses-feature below; the engine checks it at
    start, and game/data/engine.json "mobile" sets the lowest minor to 1): only Google Play filters on uses-feature, so a sideloaded APK on a phone
    that reports less starts and is told so. Landscape only, and every configuration change handled in place, because a NativeActivity that is
    recreated starts its native thread again over a running game.

    The report below: Android 11 and later can show, at the next start, the system's record of how the last run ended and the end of the game's log
    (SupersonicActivity.showReport, PostMortem.java). The log is the one main.cpp writes on a phone, <files>/Magic Portals/scratch/magicportals.log
    (Scratch::ArrangedFor puts it there first on a phone); tools/package/test_android_package.py ties this value to the C++ names it is made of.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    package="com.ivancvetanovic.magicportals">

    <uses-sdk android:minSdkVersion="26" android:targetSdkVersion="35" />

    <uses-feature android:name="android.hardware.vulkan.version" android:version="0x401000" android:required="true" />
    <uses-feature android:name="android.hardware.touchscreen" android:required="false" />
    <uses-feature android:name="android.hardware.gamepad" android:required="false" />

    <application
        android:label="Magic Portals Enhanced"
        android:icon="@mipmap/ic_launcher"
        android:hasCode="true"
        android:allowBackup="false"
        android:extractNativeLibs="true"
        android:appCategory="game"
        android:isGame="true"
        android:theme="@android:style/Theme.NoTitleBar.Fullscreen">

        <activity
            android:name="com.ivancvetanovic.supersonic.SupersonicActivity"
            android:label="Magic Portals Enhanced"
            android:exported="true"
            android:launchMode="singleTask"
            android:screenOrientation="landscape"
            android:resizeableActivity="false"
            android:configChanges="orientation|screenSize|smallestScreenSize|screenLayout|keyboard|keyboardHidden|navigation|uiMode|density|fontScale|layoutDirection|locale|touchscreen|colorMode">

            <meta-data android:name="android.app.lib_name" android:value="MagicPortals" />

            <!-- The report of a last run that ended unexpectedly, shown at the next start. -->
            <meta-data android:name="supersonic.reportUnexpectedExit" android:value="true" />
            <meta-data android:name="supersonic.reportLog" android:value="Magic Portals/scratch/magicportals.log" />
            <!-- A scripted run (it leaves this file, game/android/AndroidMain.cpp) never meets the report. -->
            <meta-data android:name="supersonic.reportSkipWhenFile" android:value="magicportals_args.txt" />

            <intent-filter>
                <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN" />
                <category android:name="android.intent.category.LAUNCHER" />
            </intent-filter>
        </activity>
    </application>
</manifest>
